  "description": "PEBLIV crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H122 O42 Tb4 Yb5 1+,H1 O1 1-,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb01 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb03 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb02 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb02? (Yb) has 0 O neighbors; Tb01? (Tb) has 0 O neighbors; Tb03? (Tb) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.542-5.065 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.46-169.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb4Yb5(acac)16(OD)10](OD).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
